WEBVTT

00:09.009 --> 00:11.052
Start from the beginning.

00:12.179 --> 00:14.431
Nothing could have prepared us
for what lay waiting.

00:17.810 --> 00:20.186
Flint's powers must have come
from the same place.

00:20.187 --> 00:22.814
I'm Mr. Byrne.
Mayor Morris forgot

00:22.815 --> 00:24.733
who runs this town.

00:24.734 --> 00:26.693
-  Four veterans from the POW camp.
-  All seen

00:26.694 --> 00:28.236
Dr. Alethea Faber.

00:28.237 --> 00:29.946
Well, what the hell are we waiting for?

00:29.947 --> 00:31.823
There's a reporter asking
to speak with you.

00:31.824 --> 00:33.992
This is my secretary Ogden.

00:33.993 --> 00:36.327
You really had no idea

00:36.328 --> 00:37.996
your patients have superpowers?

00:37.997 --> 00:39.080
Are you calling her

00:39.081 --> 00:40.206
a liar?

00:40.207 --> 00:41.916
I am sorry. I cannot help you.

00:41.917 --> 00:43.168
Faber's been looking

00:43.169 --> 00:45.336
for a cure, but she's just gonna kill him.

00:45.337 --> 00:47.046
Let me tell Cat before you print it.

00:47.047 --> 00:48.131
I'll give you a day.

00:48.132 --> 00:49.924
Flint's gonna die?

00:49.925 --> 00:53.553
What's left for us? What if we went
someplace where nobody knows us?

00:53.554 --> 00:55.388
I'm willing to take a chance and find out.

00:55.389 --> 00:57.724
If that reporter publishes,
they're coming for us.

00:57.725 --> 01:00.560
Dr. Faber,
are you really able to help them?

01:00.561 --> 01:02.312
You know who The Spider is, don't you?

01:02.313 --> 01:04.147
Ben Reilly.

02:30.276 --> 02:32.610
What the hell?

02:33.904 --> 02:35.363
Mr. Reilly.

02:35.364 --> 02:37.615
I-I'm not here to cause any trouble.

02:37.616 --> 02:40.911
I-I'd just like
a minute of your time, please.

02:41.996 --> 02:43.246
That's...

02:43.247 --> 02:46.040
That's not really necessary.

02:46.041 --> 02:48.710
I haven't had a gun in my hand
since the war.

02:48.711 --> 02:49.794
Civil War?

02:53.257 --> 02:54.883
You don't remember me.

02:54.884 --> 02:56.342
From yesterday.

02:56.343 --> 02:58.386
No. Back in France.

02:58.387 --> 03:00.471
You saved my life.

03:00.472 --> 03:02.391
What are you talking about?

03:03.726 --> 03:05.311
Easy, old man.

03:08.939 --> 03:10.857
They called me "Freckles"

03:10.858 --> 03:13.026
because I looked so young.

03:13.027 --> 03:16.697
Uh, they thought I was 15
and lied to get in the war.

03:17.281 --> 03:21.075
I suppose I was one
of the f-fortunate ones.

03:21.076 --> 03:23.119
I'm still breathing, but my mutation

03:23.120 --> 03:26.080
is aging me at a dog's clip

03:26.081 --> 03:28.792
and getting worse as it goes.

03:29.293 --> 03:34.380
Dr. Faber is my last chance to survive.

03:34.381 --> 03:36.467
She's a good woman.

03:36.967 --> 03:38.886
Trying to do a good thing.

03:41.972 --> 03:43.641
Want a drink?

03:48.562 --> 03:52.231
How old are you really?

03:52.232 --> 03:54.442
I'll be 36 in April.

03:54.443 --> 03:56.320
If I live to see it.

03:56.946 --> 03:59.280
I'm not the only one who's suffering.

03:59.281 --> 04:01.032
- Th-That's why I came here.
- If you're looking

04:01.033 --> 04:02.784
for the files, I don't have 'em.

04:02.785 --> 04:04.327
The files don't matter.

04:04.328 --> 04:07.914
I mean, not really.
They're just a laundry list of failures.

04:07.915 --> 04:10.459
D-Dead ends and dashed hopes.

04:11.043 --> 04:12.503
It's your reporter friend.

04:13.087 --> 04:15.088
If he prints that story,

04:15.089 --> 04:17.800
that's the end of Faber's work.

04:18.801 --> 04:20.426
That's the end of me.

04:22.137 --> 04:24.055
I'm sorry.

04:25.349 --> 04:26.891
But it's too late.

04:26.892 --> 04:30.144
Robbie wouldn't stop
even if I asked him to.

04:30.145 --> 04:32.773
And you-you won't even try?

04:33.440 --> 04:34.524
No.

04:34.525 --> 04:36.234
Why?

04:36.235 --> 04:39.863
I mean, don't-don't you want to see
your comrades cured?

04:40.572 --> 04:42.657
Would you want to be cured?

04:43.867 --> 04:45.535
What is that supposed to mean?

04:45.536 --> 04:47.870
Means I know who

04:47.871 --> 04:49.580
and what you really are.

04:49.581 --> 04:54.919
I followed you into that ward
that day when you and your unit saved us.

04:54.920 --> 04:57.422
That day when that thing...

04:57.423 --> 04:58.673
bit you.

04:58.674 --> 05:00.633
If you hadn't changed your name,

05:00.634 --> 05:04.263
I would have come knocking
at your door years ago.

05:06.682 --> 05:08.350
Dementia hit early, huh?

05:09.018 --> 05:10.227
Don't do that.

05:10.894 --> 05:13.646
I can excuse a lot,
but I deserve better than that.

05:13.647 --> 05:17.316
You're delivering me a death sentence.

05:17.317 --> 05:19.945
At least have the decency to be honest.

05:30.456 --> 05:34.250
Truth is this is a part of me
I wish never existed.

05:34.251 --> 05:36.377
And as of tomorrow,

05:36.378 --> 05:37.920
it no longer does.

05:37.921 --> 05:40.214
I'm leaving town. Starting over.

05:40.215 --> 05:41.467
As Ben Reilly.

05:43.844 --> 05:45.678
I'm sorry, Freckles. I...

05:45.679 --> 05:47.722
I wish I could offer you the same chance.

05:47.723 --> 05:49.724
That's it?

05:49.725 --> 05:52.393
I-I-I can't change your mind?

05:52.394 --> 05:54.021
Been a long time coming.

05:55.522 --> 05:57.900
I-I wish it didn't have to be this way.

06:02.780 --> 06:04.113
What did you...

06:31.225 --> 06:33.893
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

06:33.894 --> 06:35.645
♪ I could tell the story ♪

06:35.646 --> 06:38.314
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

06:38.315 --> 06:41.109
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

06:41.110 --> 06:43.194
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

06:43.195 --> 06:45.655
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

06:45.656 --> 06:48.866
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

06:48.867 --> 06:52.203
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

06:52.204 --> 06:55.331
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

06:55.332 --> 06:58.793
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

06:58.794 --> 07:02.004
♪ Hey, lover ♪

07:02.005 --> 07:04.882
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

07:04.883 --> 07:07.135
♪ from all the pain ♪

07:07.136 --> 07:09.595
♪ I suffer ♪

07:09.596 --> 07:12.431
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

07:12.432 --> 07:15.977
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

07:15.978 --> 07:18.354
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

07:18.355 --> 07:19.730
♪ But you could be ♪

07:19.731 --> 07:22.943
♪ my saving grace ♪

08:45.442 --> 08:47.568
There we are.

08:47.569 --> 08:49.070
Stay calm, Mr. Reilly.

08:49.071 --> 08:50.905
Deep breaths.

08:50.906 --> 08:54.200
Took quite a lot of secobarbital
to keep you sedated.

08:54.201 --> 08:56.285
I'm sure you must feel pretty rotten.

08:56.286 --> 08:58.246
Wh-Where am I?

08:58.247 --> 09:00.457
My private laboratory.

09:01.917 --> 09:03.751
Wh-What is this? Why am I--

09:03.752 --> 09:06.170
Oh, everything's okay, Mr. Reilly.

09:06.171 --> 09:08.631
I just need to run some preliminary tests.

09:08.632 --> 09:10.967
Investigations into your blood makeup,

09:10.968 --> 09:13.135
your proteins, your genetic material.

09:13.136 --> 09:14.137
Uncuff me.

09:14.721 --> 09:17.515
Trust me, this will all be a lot easier

09:17.516 --> 09:19.517
if you calm down and let me do my work.

09:19.518 --> 09:20.685
Work?

09:20.686 --> 09:22.436
Mr. Reilly, you broke into my office

09:22.437 --> 09:25.356
and stole my most important files.

09:25.357 --> 09:26.858
Did you read the files?

09:27.484 --> 09:29.235
- Yes.
- Then you know who I am

09:29.236 --> 09:30.528
and what I'm doing.

09:30.529 --> 09:33.197
And I know who you are, too, Mr. Spider.

09:33.198 --> 09:34.740
So let's not play games.

09:34.741 --> 09:37.702
I have a lot of work to do
and not a lot of time to do it.

09:37.703 --> 09:38.786
Are we clear?

09:38.787 --> 09:40.871
Let me go and I won't kill you.

09:40.872 --> 09:44.125
No. Threats like that are why we need
to keep you restrained.

09:44.126 --> 09:46.294
It’s not a threat, it's a promise.

09:46.295 --> 09:48.421
You're very convincing.

09:48.422 --> 09:50.339
But we know what type of man
you really are.

09:50.340 --> 09:53.009
You ran into danger

09:53.010 --> 09:55.636
to liberate a camp of tortured soldiers.

09:55.637 --> 09:57.805
You saved Ogden's life.

09:57.806 --> 10:00.308
- Yes.
- And then you came home

10:00.309 --> 10:02.101
and chose to save a lot more.

10:02.102 --> 10:04.687
You're not a murderer. You're a hero.

10:08.483 --> 10:09.775
You'll never break those.

10:09.776 --> 10:12.778
We have enough drugs in you
to weaken King Kong.

10:12.779 --> 10:14.989
Now I'm simply going to draw some blood.

10:14.990 --> 10:16.658
A child can sit through this.

10:17.159 --> 10:19.786
Ogden, prep the blood draw
and retrieval kits.

10:21.371 --> 10:23.497
This won't do you any good.

10:23.498 --> 10:25.292
I've been here before.

10:27.002 --> 10:28.670
Jones! Jones!

12:15.902 --> 12:17.445
At ease, Soldier.

12:19.114 --> 12:20.906
Sit. Sit.

12:23.493 --> 12:24.910
You okay?

12:24.911 --> 12:26.412
In a fair amount of pain, I hear.

12:26.413 --> 12:29.415
Nothing...
I can't...  handle, sir.

12:29.416 --> 12:30.833
Glad to hear it.

12:30.834 --> 12:33.419
The most important thing
is to get you comfortable.

12:33.420 --> 12:36.172
The good news is you've got the finest
medical team in the whole world

12:36.173 --> 12:38.549
all 100% focused on you.

12:38.550 --> 12:40.301
You can't beat that, can you?

12:40.302 --> 12:42.761
No, sir.

12:42.762 --> 12:44.263
Get him a pop.

12:44.264 --> 12:45.973
Chocolate bar. Anything he needs, okay?

12:45.974 --> 12:47.475
- Yes, sir.
- What...

12:49.186 --> 12:51.771
What is happening...
to me...  sir?

12:53.190 --> 12:55.691
I think we're all wondering that.

12:55.692 --> 12:58.195
But we'll get to the bottom of it,
don't you worry.

13:00.030 --> 13:01.697
They cut me open,

13:01.698 --> 13:03.240
pulled me apart,

13:03.241 --> 13:04.325
put me back together.

13:04.326 --> 13:05.701
They didn't learn a thing.

13:05.702 --> 13:08.537
I know every detail
of the Army's examination.

13:08.538 --> 13:10.748
I have studied their findings
exhaustively.

13:10.749 --> 13:12.541
But that was a long time ago.

13:12.542 --> 13:15.169
The science has advanced
by leaps and bounds.

13:15.170 --> 13:16.254
You're one of 'em.

13:16.838 --> 13:18.839
Don't you dare

13:18.840 --> 13:20.799
confuse me with them.

13:20.800 --> 13:23.427
Those scientists only cared about war.

13:23.428 --> 13:25.429
They took one look at you,

13:25.430 --> 13:26.555
and they were just like the Germans.

13:26.556 --> 13:28.849
They wanted to use you as weapons.

13:28.850 --> 13:31.393
I am trying to do the opposite.

13:32.479 --> 13:34.355
This...

13:34.356 --> 13:35.440
is personal.

13:36.107 --> 13:37.108
Yes.

13:37.692 --> 13:39.194
You lost someone.

13:40.654 --> 13:41.821
My son.

13:42.405 --> 13:44.282
Have you ever lost someone, Mr. Reilly?

13:45.283 --> 13:49.453
Someone so close to you that
it felt like a part of you was gone, too?

13:49.454 --> 13:50.579
Yes.

13:50.580 --> 13:53.415
Well, what if you could have done
something about it?

13:53.416 --> 13:55.543
What if you knew that you were losing them

13:55.544 --> 13:58.420
but that the power to change that,

13:58.421 --> 14:01.174
to save them, lay in your hands?

14:01.841 --> 14:03.510
Wouldn't you do it?

14:04.094 --> 14:06.929
Wouldn't you try everything?

14:21.278 --> 14:24.072
You can't bring your loved one back,
Mr. Reilly, but I can.

14:24.656 --> 14:26.283
Is that so much to ask?

14:26.783 --> 14:28.701
A second chance

14:28.702 --> 14:29.994
for my son?

14:39.921 --> 14:41.589
Now you understand.

14:41.590 --> 14:43.215
There's nothing I won't do

14:43.216 --> 14:44.426
to keep him alive.

14:45.427 --> 14:48.554
Your friend and I have that in common.

14:49.723 --> 14:51.223
- My friend?
- The woman

14:51.224 --> 14:52.683
who told me how to find you.

14:52.684 --> 14:55.811
She also has someone
that she is desperate to save.

14:59.316 --> 15:01.776
- Cat.
- She's quite beautiful.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.612
And determined.

15:04.613 --> 15:06.238
I'm...

15:06.239 --> 15:07.490
s-scared.

15:08.533 --> 15:09.617
Is he okay?

15:11.077 --> 15:12.328
Mr. Reilly.

15:12.329 --> 15:14.372
- Mr. Reilly.
- It's the blood loss.

15:14.956 --> 15:17.667
He'll have time to recuperate
while we run the tests.

15:31.890 --> 15:33.140
Anything?

15:33.141 --> 15:35.225
Platelet counts,
erythrocytes, hemoglobin...

15:35.226 --> 15:38.897
His blood is utterly, completely,
maddeningly normal.

15:39.689 --> 15:42.107
Look, we know he's different.

15:42.108 --> 15:45.070
The answer is somewhere inside his body.

15:46.488 --> 15:47.989
We just have to find it.

16:17.227 --> 16:18.727
Oh, good.

16:18.728 --> 16:20.479
You're awake.

16:20.480 --> 16:21.898
How are you feeling?

16:23.233 --> 16:24.983
I-I'm sorry

16:24.984 --> 16:26.276
about all this.

16:26.277 --> 16:27.487
I-I-I mean it.

16:28.154 --> 16:30.198
You-you gave me no option.

16:30.699 --> 16:32.282
Here, uh, drink this.

16:32.283 --> 16:34.034
You-you-you must be thirsty.

16:34.035 --> 16:36.036
No, it's-it's-it's water.

16:36.037 --> 16:37.622
I-I-I promise.

16:46.881 --> 16:47.965
Wow.

16:49.426 --> 16:51.177
You were thirsty.

16:52.554 --> 16:54.346
So,

16:54.347 --> 16:57.224
you were just going to leave town.

16:57.225 --> 17:00.894
Even after I told you
that there was a chance that...

17:00.895 --> 17:02.855
you could save me

17:02.856 --> 17:04.023
and the others.

17:05.567 --> 17:07.485
Spider was never a hero.

17:08.486 --> 17:10.696
I only did it for the thrill.

17:10.697 --> 17:12.073
Well...

17:12.574 --> 17:14.868
...maybe you weren't then.

17:15.785 --> 17:18.829
But there's still time
for you to become one.

17:18.830 --> 17:21.331
I'm never getting out of here alive.

17:21.332 --> 17:22.917
What are you talking about?

17:23.543 --> 17:26.378
Your mother is insane.

17:26.379 --> 17:27.755
No. No.

17:27.756 --> 17:29.131
That's not true.

17:29.132 --> 17:31.800
She's... just trying to save me.

17:31.801 --> 17:33.886
No, she's insane.

17:33.887 --> 17:35.679
I'm sorry to report

17:35.680 --> 17:37.766
that your blood samples weren't enough.

17:38.266 --> 17:41.560
I'm going to have to harvest
genetic material from your organs.

17:41.561 --> 17:44.688
Stop! If you haven't found an answer,

17:44.689 --> 17:46.399
it's because there isn't one.

17:46.983 --> 17:48.400
I will never stop.

17:48.401 --> 17:52.154
What kind of a mother would I be
if I didn’t exhaust every option?

17:52.155 --> 17:54.364
There's always an answer, Mr. Reilly.

17:54.365 --> 17:55.991
What is that?

17:55.992 --> 17:57.786
What-what-what is that?

18:05.335 --> 18:06.795
Help me, Ogden.

18:14.385 --> 18:17.555
Science is about uncovering
discernible facts.

18:18.640 --> 18:21.058
Now, the program
that the Germans conducted altered

18:21.059 --> 18:23.144
their subjects' genetic makeup.

18:24.229 --> 18:25.896
Led to corrosion,

18:25.897 --> 18:27.357
decay, instability.

18:28.358 --> 18:33.737
For some reason, you were the only subject
who gained power without degradation.

18:33.738 --> 18:36.448
Where are you taking me?

18:38.952 --> 18:40.328
He's trying to say something.

18:43.122 --> 18:44.373
I like...

18:44.374 --> 18:45.625
ravioli.

18:46.209 --> 18:48.293
You will have ravioli.

18:48.294 --> 18:51.130
All the ravioli you want.

18:54.634 --> 18:58.053
I believe that whatever process
that allowed the mutation

18:58.054 --> 18:59.972
to stabilize within your body

18:59.973 --> 19:03.852
can be retrofitted
to fully cure the other mutations.

19:06.479 --> 19:10.191
You're going to have
a nice rest now, Mr. Reilly.

19:11.276 --> 19:12.694
Mask, Ogden.

19:15.196 --> 19:16.655
Just breathe.

19:16.656 --> 19:18.615
Breathe deeply.

19:18.616 --> 19:19.950
That's good.

19:19.951 --> 19:21.660
Ten,

19:21.661 --> 19:23.036
nine,

19:23.037 --> 19:24.621
eight,

19:24.622 --> 19:26.206
seven,

19:26.207 --> 19:27.291
six...

19:35.592 --> 19:37.467
Cut him open.

19:37.468 --> 19:39.095
Let's see what he's made of.

20:10.335 --> 20:11.793
Ruby.

20:11.794 --> 20:13.128
Yeah, you ding-a-ling.

20:13.129 --> 20:14.671
Were you expecting someone else?

20:14.672 --> 20:16.506
I missed you so much.

20:16.507 --> 20:18.091
Oh, Ruby.

20:18.092 --> 20:21.303
Ruby, Ruby, Ruby.

20:28.394 --> 20:31.356
Hey, Reilly.
Thought you could get rid of me?

20:31.940 --> 20:34.358
You're nothing without me.

20:58.257 --> 21:01.219
You son of a bitch. You set me up.

21:03.429 --> 21:04.846
You're a coward, Reilly.

21:04.847 --> 21:07.225
Fortune favors the bold.

21:07.809 --> 21:09.811
I tried to warn you.

21:10.603 --> 21:12.814
Now you're gonna burn.

22:00.403 --> 22:01.988
Oh, my God.

23:21.901 --> 23:24.319
It's time.

23:24.320 --> 23:26.571
Are you ready?

23:26.572 --> 23:27.990
Yeah.

23:30.451 --> 23:31.661
What's wrong?

23:33.788 --> 23:35.622
Are you sure this is gonna work?

23:35.623 --> 23:38.500
- I mean, what-what if--
- I am as sure

23:38.501 --> 23:40.920
as I've ever been. All right?

23:43.548 --> 23:44.966
Okay.

23:46.050 --> 23:47.593
I'm ready.

23:48.594 --> 23:50.762
- It's already done.
- Ah.

24:28.217 --> 24:29.551
Oh, oh.

24:29.552 --> 24:30.886
Oh! Mm.

24:34.432 --> 24:35.433
Oh.

24:40.396 --> 24:41.771
You did it.

24:41.772 --> 24:43.733
- You really did it.
- Mm-hmm.

24:45.568 --> 24:47.611
I cannot believe it.

24:47.612 --> 24:49.279
Oh...

24:49.280 --> 24:52.032
My little Freckles.

24:52.033 --> 24:54.284
Oh. All right.

24:54.285 --> 24:55.952
Robertson will have published
his story by now,

24:55.953 --> 24:59.915
so we-we need to clear this place out
and get out of here.

24:59.916 --> 25:01.334
Wh...

25:02.460 --> 25:04.545
We need to give Reilly the antidote first.

25:07.423 --> 25:08.716
We can't do that, Oggie.

25:09.342 --> 25:10.634
We kidnapped him.

25:10.635 --> 25:13.471
We operated on him against his will.

25:14.805 --> 25:16.723
The best thing for us,
the only hope for us

25:16.724 --> 25:18.642
is to just become different people.

25:18.643 --> 25:22.647
To disappear with no one left
who knows anything about us.

25:28.736 --> 25:29.903
What are you saying?

25:33.741 --> 25:34.867
No.

25:35.451 --> 25:37.077
They will throw us both in prison.

25:37.078 --> 25:40.705
I have not spent
the last 15 years of my life

25:40.706 --> 25:42.290
trying to give you your life back

25:42.291 --> 25:45.335
just to have you waste away
in a jail cell.

25:45.336 --> 25:47.671
I'm sorry, Ogden.

25:47.672 --> 25:51.092
His life was always the price of yours.

25:58.349 --> 26:00.267
I'll do it.

26:00.268 --> 26:03.895
- Ogden--
- After everything we've both been through,

26:03.896 --> 26:08.651
I need to look him in the eye,
soldier-to-soldier.

26:10.736 --> 26:12.279
Okay.

26:34.468 --> 26:37.096
I feel like a young boy
on a Christmas morning.

26:38.180 --> 26:41.891
If this doctor can give us the name
of every superpowered man from that camp,

26:41.892 --> 26:44.145
we'll have an army nobody can stop.

26:44.729 --> 26:47.397
Not even the goddamn Spider.

26:47.398 --> 26:50.026
The suffering they put you through...

26:51.444 --> 26:53.070
...they'll rue the day.

27:56.133 --> 27:57.385
Ah...

28:02.515 --> 28:03.808
Don't.

28:09.605 --> 28:11.523
Ogden?

28:11.524 --> 28:13.108
You were right.

28:13.109 --> 28:15.027
She sent me to kill you.

28:15.611 --> 28:17.487
But you saved my life.

28:17.488 --> 28:19.656
Least I can do is try to save yours.

28:21.242 --> 28:24.537
Just promise me you won't hurt her.

28:25.538 --> 28:27.705
Yeah, I'm not the one with the gun.

28:27.706 --> 28:29.916
I'm not the one with the spider powers.

28:29.917 --> 28:34.422
I'm just trying to get home.

28:37.716 --> 28:39.175
Let's get you home.

29:01.991 --> 29:04.702
These doors are getting bigger and bigger.

29:20.885 --> 29:22.260
Wow.

29:22.261 --> 29:24.429
Look at you.

29:24.430 --> 29:26.181
Marvelous. Just marvelous.

29:26.182 --> 29:27.724
You're back.

29:27.725 --> 29:29.309
What are your plans?

29:29.310 --> 29:30.518
Pardon me?

29:30.519 --> 29:32.228
Well, now that you've got your life back,

29:32.229 --> 29:35.398
what are you planning
on doing with it, Freckles?

29:35.399 --> 29:37.942
I don't know. Uh...

29:37.943 --> 29:39.652
Huh, I...

29:39.653 --> 29:41.613
I've been preparing to die for so long,

29:41.614 --> 29:43.823
I never really thought about how to live.

29:43.824 --> 29:45.325
Are you, are you okay?

29:45.326 --> 29:46.743
What day is it?

29:46.744 --> 29:48.286
- Excuse me?
- The day, the day.

29:48.287 --> 29:49.787
What's today?

29:49.788 --> 29:51.915
Monday. Uh, M-Monday afternoon.

29:51.916 --> 29:53.374
Oh, poo.

29:53.375 --> 29:55.210
Robbie's chasing his Pulitzer.

29:55.211 --> 29:56.878
He's published the location of the lab.

29:56.879 --> 29:58.463
They'll be here any second.

30:04.512 --> 30:06.304
How many do you think there are?

30:06.305 --> 30:07.722
Hard to say.

30:07.723 --> 30:09.140
There were dozens of us at the camp.

30:09.141 --> 30:12.519
Imagine a lot
made their way back to New York.

30:12.520 --> 30:16.357
Anybody had any trouble over the years
would've found their way to Faber.

30:40.005 --> 30:41.214
You okay?

30:41.215 --> 30:43.216
What's it look like? I'm fine.

30:43.217 --> 30:44.801
Oh.

30:44.802 --> 30:46.971
Cherry red. My favorite.

30:52.059 --> 30:54.395
It's up and through there.

30:57.565 --> 30:58.774
You're not coming?

31:00.526 --> 31:01.818
I'm not leaving her.

31:02.987 --> 31:04.822
You can't beat those guys.

31:05.406 --> 31:06.949
You're probably right.

31:09.410 --> 31:11.036
But she's my mom.

31:34.059 --> 31:35.269
Up you get.

31:36.520 --> 31:38.521
What's the matter, Doc?

31:38.522 --> 31:40.315
You don't look that thrilled to see us.

31:40.316 --> 31:41.941
I'm sorry,
I'm-I'm just surprised.

31:41.942 --> 31:43.359
'Cause your secret lab's

31:43.360 --> 31:44.862
not a secret no more?

31:45.946 --> 31:47.405
So, we're monsters,

31:47.406 --> 31:48.906
are we?

31:48.907 --> 31:50.825
Quite the operation
you've got

31:50.826 --> 31:52.243
going down here.

31:52.244 --> 31:55.204
Everything but a cauldron
and two weird sisters.

31:55.205 --> 31:56.497
That story says you did this to us.

31:56.498 --> 32:00.168
No, absolutely not. Quite the opposite.

32:00.169 --> 32:01.878
- Liar, liar.
-  All right.

32:01.879 --> 32:04.214
Hold your horses. Everybody.

32:05.716 --> 32:08.718
Now we'll all have a conversation.

32:08.719 --> 32:10.219
Nice and civilized.

32:10.220 --> 32:11.804
- Right, Doc?
- Of course.

32:11.805 --> 32:14.057
Very pleased
to make your acquaintance, Doctor.

32:14.058 --> 32:16.184
- Do you know who I am?
- Yes.

32:16.185 --> 32:18.895
Good. Now tell the boys
you're not in the business

32:18.896 --> 32:20.897
- of making monsters.
- No.

32:20.898 --> 32:24.359
No. All I have ever tried to do
is to help you all.

32:24.360 --> 32:27.070
- Every one of you.
- Hey, how is old Oggie, huh?

32:27.071 --> 32:29.405
He finally kick
the proverbial bucket or what?

32:30.532 --> 32:32.075
Sadly, yes.

32:32.076 --> 32:35.703
Now, my friends here
say you've been treating

32:35.704 --> 32:37.288
their various maladies.

32:37.289 --> 32:42.086
I'm curious to know
if there are others like them.

32:43.170 --> 32:45.046
Yes.

32:45.047 --> 32:47.298
I could take you to them now.

32:47.299 --> 32:50.677
Oh, they're here? Even better.

32:50.678 --> 32:52.638
Lead on, my dear.

33:49.862 --> 33:51.280
My God.

34:04.168 --> 34:05.711
What is all this?

34:07.129 --> 34:09.422
- They're all dead?
-  I did my best,

34:09.423 --> 34:11.174
but they succumbed to their mutations

34:11.175 --> 34:13.259
before I'd figured out a way to save them.

34:13.260 --> 34:15.595
And then you put them in jars
like a bunch of freaks?

34:15.596 --> 34:17.848
-  No, that is--
- It's Johnny.

34:20.225 --> 34:21.852
Johnny Forte.

34:50.672 --> 34:52.256
You never cared about us.

34:52.257 --> 34:53.758
That is not true.

34:53.759 --> 34:55.802
You know what it's been like?
Living like this?

34:55.803 --> 34:57.470
- Please...
- Our bodies somehow stronger

34:57.471 --> 34:58.679
and weaker at the same time?

34:58.680 --> 35:00.723
- The world calling us monsters.
- Please listen.

35:00.724 --> 35:04.101
I have finally figured it out.

35:04.102 --> 35:07.855
I promise you I can help you all,
if you will just let me.

35:07.856 --> 35:09.899
Help us?

35:09.900 --> 35:11.276
You mean like you helped them?

35:12.361 --> 35:14.695
These men was our comrades.

35:14.696 --> 35:16.239
Our brothers.

35:16.240 --> 35:18.658
We fought with these men.

35:18.659 --> 35:21.161
We suffered with these men.

35:33.966 --> 35:35.675
Wait.

35:35.676 --> 35:37.093
Wait, I know you.

35:38.595 --> 35:40.305
We were in the cell together.

35:41.431 --> 35:43.474
I grabbed the guard,

35:43.475 --> 35:44.893
you put the knife in.

35:47.855 --> 35:49.940
Nobody shoots me, you little bastard.

35:52.442 --> 35:54.152
Dirk, stop! What are you doing?

35:56.446 --> 35:58.240
Get off of me.

36:09.877 --> 36:11.252
There's nothing here for us.

36:11.253 --> 36:12.671
Let's go.

36:16.049 --> 36:20.553
You're going to have to learn
some impulse control, son.

36:31.106 --> 36:32.356
-  Hey.
-  Hmm?

36:32.357 --> 36:35.443
-  You got shit in your teeth.
-  Oh, no.

36:35.444 --> 36:37.111
- I look so dumb.
- Yeah, you look real stupid.

36:37.112 --> 36:39.280
I was in the car
with those guys for an hour.

36:39.281 --> 36:40.990
-  Now, don't bite my finger.
-  You think they saw?

36:40.991 --> 36:43.326
Yeah. Right back here.

36:43.327 --> 36:45.328
- Yeah.
-  Did you get it?

36:45.329 --> 36:47.204
You know, I wanted
to be a dentist when I was a kid.

36:47.205 --> 36:48.873
-  Oh, yeah?
- Yeah. I got it--

36:50.042 --> 36:53.085
God! The hell was that?
